{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)"},"metadata":{"title":"reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reconcile","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV","text":"EntityStore","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleting","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"preserving","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"symbolKind":"method","roleHeading":"Instance Method","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"externalID":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV9reconcile4with8deleting10preservingyACyxG_Shy10Foundation4UUIDVGALtF"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reconciles this store against a snapshot covering only "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"some"}]},{"type":"text","text":" of its IDs."}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"mutating","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"reconcile","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"with","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"remote","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux11EntityStoreV","text":"EntityStore","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Entity","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deleting","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"deletedIDs","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"preserving","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sh","text":"Set","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:10Foundation4UUIDV","text":"UUID","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">)","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"parameters":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The rows read from storage for the IDs in question. Rows for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"IDs the caller didn’t ask about are simply not here, and their"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"absence means nothing."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"remote"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs storage reports as deleted elsewhere. Removed with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same origin a full reconcile uses, so no deletion is recorded and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"none is echoed back to the store it came from. An ID that "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still holds is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" removed however it is named here: a live row"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is positive evidence, and a tombstone can be stale."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"deletedIDs"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"IDs the caller knows carry unflushed local intent, exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as in the full reconcile. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remote"},{"type":"text","text":" has no authority over them, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"neither does "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deletedIDs"},{"type":"text","text":". This store’s own un-drained "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/changes","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"folded in automatically.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"preserving"}],"kind":"parameters"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The counterpart to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore\/reconcile(with:preserving:removingMissing:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"partial read — a refresh of the rows a sync tick reported as changed,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"rather than of the whole table. Absorbing rows works identically; what","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"changes is where deletions come from."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A partial snapshot "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"cannot","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" infer deletion from absence. An ID missing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"from it was not deleted, it was not asked for, and treating the two alike","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"would empty the store on the first partial merge. So removal is driven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entirely by ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"deletedIDs"},{"type":"text","text":", which the caller must have positive evidence"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for — a history tombstone, not an empty result.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Does ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" record changes — this is a hydration operation, for the same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason the full reconcile isn’t one.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/reconcile(with:deleting:preserving:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","kind":"symbol","title":"Swidux","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"role":"symbol","title":"EntityStore","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","abstract":[{"text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"every mutation for downstream persistence.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","type":"topic"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore/changes":{"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore\/changes","title":"changes","identifier":"do